From d24ce9a2aa1aeba440bb2fd17eebbc90f5c05a3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 10:42:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/31] a210: vendor import: 10-thead-drivers

Cherry-picked vendor enablement group 10 (10-thead-drivers) onto Linux v6.6.141 as
the maintained A210 LTS branch (one commit per kernel/patches group). Applied
with git apply --recount; reconciled against vendor branch osl/a210-v2.9.0.
See kernel/patches/README.md and kernel/T2-DESIGN.md for group rationale.

v7.0 port adaptations: dropped the vendor riscv-iommu (drivers/iommu/riscv/,
incl. io_pgtable.c and iommu-sysfs.c) and the vendor dwmac-thead.c in favor
of the equivalents upstream has since merged; united drivers/clk/thead
Kconfig/Makefile with upstream CLK_THEAD_TH1520_AP. The A210 DT node
(zhihe,iommu) will be disabled in the DTS commit -- direct DMA, matching
U-Boot behavior.

Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
